sol:'The dipole operator $\\vec{r}$ is a rank-1 object: by the triangle rule it can only couple states whose $l$ differs by exactly one (parity flips too, since $\\vec{r}$ is odd). Hence $s \\leftrightarrow p$, $p \\leftrightarrow d$ are allowed while $s \\leftrightarrow s$ or $p \\leftrightarrow p$ are forbidden at E1 order — atoms may cheat via the far weaker magnetic-dipole or quadrupole channels.',
